    "description": "Section heading: privacy of GhostScan and the Scan bubble"
  },
  "helpGuideScanBubblePrivacyBullet1": "The screen is captured only when you tap the bubble or the GhostScan tile, and Android asks you first.",
  "@helpGuideScanBubblePrivacyBullet1": {
    "description": "Privacy: the screen is captured only when you ask"
  },
  "helpGuideScanBubblePrivacyBullet2": "The code is read on your phone. Nothing is sent online for reading.",
  "@helpGuideScanBubblePrivacyBullet2": {
    "description": "Privacy: the code is read on the phone"
  },
  "helpGuideScanBubblePrivacyBullet3": "The screen picture is not saved to your gallery and is deleted right after reading.",
  "@helpGuideScanBubblePrivacyBullet3": {
    "description": "Privacy: the screen picture is deleted after reading"
  },
  "helpGuideScanBubbleLimitsTitle": "Good to know",
  "@helpGuideScanBubbleLimitsTitle": {
    "description": "Section heading: limits of GhostScan and the Scan bubble"
  },
  "helpGuideScanBubbleLimitsBullet1": "On Android 14 and newer, Android asks for screen capture permission on every tap.",
  "@helpGuideScanBubbleLimitsBullet1": {
    "description": "Limits: Android 14 asks on every tap"
  },
  "helpGuideScanBubbleLimitsBullet2": "Banking, payment and some video apps block screen capture. Codes inside them cannot be read.",
  "@helpGuideScanBubbleLimitsBullet2": {
    "description": "Limits: some apps block screen capture"
  },
  "helpGuideScanBubbleLimitsBullet3": "Some phones have extra \"pop-up window\" or battery settings that can hide or stop the bubble.",
  "@helpGuideScanBubbleLimitsBullet3": {
    "description": "Limits: some phones have extra settings that stop the bubble"
  },
  "helpGuideScanBubbleTip": "Tip: Add the Scan bubble tile to Quick Settings. Then one tap turns the bubble on or off from any app.",
  "@helpGuideScanBubbleTip": {
    "description": "Tip at the end of the guide on scanning codes shown in other apps"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeName": "Making codes (CodeForge)",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeName": {
    "description": "Help hub card title for the CodeForge guide"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeSummary": "Make your own QR codes and barcodes, change their look, and share them.",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeSummary": {
    "description": "Help hub card summary for the CodeForge guide"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeIntro": "CodeForge lets you make your own QR code or barcode: for your Wi-Fi, your contact details, a link, a UPI payment and more. You can change its colours and shapes, and share it as a picture.",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeIntro": {
    "description": "Opening paragraph of the CodeForge guide"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeTypeTitle": "1. Choose what to put in it",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeTypeTitle": {
    "description": "CodeForge guide section heading: choosing what the code holds"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeTypeBullet1": "Open the CodeForge tab at the bottom of the screen.",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeTypeBullet1": {
    "description": "CodeForge guide: opening the CodeForge tab"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeTypeBullet2": "Pick the code type: QR Code, or a barcode such as Code 128, EAN-13, EAN-8, UPC-A, Code 39, PDF417 or Data Matrix.",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeTypeBullet2": {
    "description": "CodeForge guide: choosing a QR code or a barcode type"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeTypeBullet3": "For a QR code, pick what it holds: Text, URL / Link, Wi-Fi, Contact, UPI Pay, SMS, Email or Location.",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeTypeBullet3": {
    "description": "CodeForge guide: the kinds of content a QR code can hold"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeTypeBullet4": "Fill in the boxes. The preview changes as you type.",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeTypeBullet4": {
    "description": "CodeForge guide: filling in the boxes and the live preview"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeTypeBullet5": "For text, you can also tap Read from file to load text from a file (up to 500 characters).",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeTypeBullet5": {
    "description": "CodeForge guide: reading text from a file"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeTypeBullet6": "For a location, tap Use My Location to fill in where you are. The app asks for your location only at that moment and does not keep it.",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeTypeBullet6": {
    "description": "CodeForge guide: filling a location with the current place"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeStyleTitle": "2. Change the look",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeStyleTitle": {
    "description": "CodeForge guide section heading: changing the look of the code"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeStyleBullet1": "Design & Structure: choose the shape of the big corner squares, their centres, and the small dots.",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeStyleBullet1": {
    "description": "CodeForge guide: the shape choices"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeStyleBullet2": "Colors & Gradients: choose the code colour and the background, or a colour blend such as Sunset or Ocean.",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeStyleBullet2": {
    "description": "CodeForge guide: the colour choices"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeStyleBullet3": "Keep strong contrast. A dark code on a light background scans best.",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeStyleBullet3": {
    "description": "CodeForge guide: keep strong contrast so the code scans"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeStyleBullet4": "Center Badge: put a small icon in the middle of the code.",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeStyleBullet4": {
    "description": "CodeForge guide: the centre badge"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeStyleBullet5": "Error Correction: how much damage the code can take and still scan. L survives about 7%, M 15%, Q 25% and H 30%. Higher levels make the code busier. Choose H when you add a centre badge.",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeStyleBullet5": {
    "description": "CodeForge guide: error correction levels explained simply"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeStyleBullet6": "Show Text Label prints the text under a barcode. Reset Styling puts the look back to normal.",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeStyleBullet6": {
    "description": "CodeForge guide: the text label under a barcode and the reset button"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeShareTitle": "3. Check and share",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeShareTitle": {
    "description": "CodeForge guide section heading: checking and sharing the code"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeShareBullet1": "For a link, tap Check to test the link for safety before you share it.",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeShareBullet1": {
    "description": "CodeForge guide: checking a link before sharing"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeShareBullet2": "Tap Share PNG to share it as a normal picture, or Share SVG for a sharp picture that prints well at any size.",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeShareBullet2": {
    "description": "CodeForge guide: sharing as PNG or SVG"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeShareBullet3": "Tap Copy Content to copy the text inside the code.",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeShareBullet3": {
    "description": "CodeForge guide: copying the content of the code"
  },
  "helpGuideCodeForgeTip": "Tip: Before you print many copies, scan your new code once with this app to make sure it reads well.",
  "@helpGuideCodeForgeTip": {
    "description": "Tip at the end of the CodeForge guide"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrName": "AirQR: send data with no network",
  "@helpGuideAirQrName": {
    "description": "Help hub card title for the AirQR guide"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrSummary": "Send text, or move your app data to another phone, using moving QR codes. No Wi-Fi, Bluetooth or cables.",
  "@helpGuideAirQrSummary": {
    "description": "Help hub card summary for the AirQR guide"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrIntro": "AirQR sends data from one phone to another using only the screen and the camera. The sending phone shows a fast series of QR codes. The receiving phone watches them and joins them back together. No network is used at all.",
  "@helpGuideAirQrIntro": {
    "description": "Opening paragraph of the AirQR guide"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrStreamingTitle": "How to send",
  "@helpGuideAirQrStreamingTitle": {
    "description": "AirQR guide section heading: how to send"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrStreamingBullet1": "On the sending phone, open Scan > More options > AirQR receiver, then tap the AirQR transmitter button at the top.",
  "@helpGuideAirQrStreamingBullet1": {
    "description": "AirQR guide: opening the transmitter"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrStreamingBullet2": "Type or paste what you want to send under Data to send.",
  "@helpGuideAirQrStreamingBullet2": {
    "description": "AirQR guide: entering the data to send"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrStreamingBullet3": "Choose the Stream Speed (5 to 25 frames a second), then tap Start stream.",
  "@helpGuideAirQrStreamingBullet3": {
    "description": "AirQR guide: choosing the speed and starting"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrStreamingBullet4": "Keep the sending screen bright and hold it still.",
  "@helpGuideAirQrStreamingBullet4": {
    "description": "AirQR guide: keep the sending screen bright and still"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrControlsTitle": "How to receive",
  "@helpGuideAirQrControlsTitle": {
    "description": "AirQR guide section heading: how to receive"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrControlsBullet1": "On the other phone, open Scan > More options > AirQR receiver and point the camera at the sending screen.",
  "@helpGuideAirQrControlsBullet1": {
    "description": "AirQR guide: opening the receiver"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrControlsBullet2": "A progress bar shows how many parts have arrived and how many are still missing.",
  "@helpGuideAirQrControlsBullet2": {
    "description": "AirQR guide: the progress bar"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrControlsBullet3": "Missed parts are no problem. AirQR also sends extra repair parts, so the receiver can fill in the gaps.",
  "@helpGuideAirQrControlsBullet3": {
    "description": "AirQR guide: missed parts are repaired by extra frames"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrControlsBullet4": "When all parts arrive, the app checks the data and shows Transfer complete! You can copy the data from there.",
  "@helpGuideAirQrControlsBullet4": {
    "description": "AirQR guide: the transfer complete screen"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrSyncTitle": "Move your data to a new phone",
  "@helpGuideAirQrSyncTitle": {
    "description": "AirQR guide section heading: moving app data to a new phone"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrSyncBullet1": "On the old phone, go to Settings > AirQR Optical Sync. Choose your history, your app settings, or both.",
  "@helpGuideAirQrSyncBullet1": {
    "description": "AirQR guide: starting a device sync on the old phone"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrSyncBullet2": "Type a passphrase or PIN, or tap Generate PIN. This locks the data, so only someone with the PIN can open it.",
  "@helpGuideAirQrSyncBullet2": {
    "description": "AirQR guide: locking the sync with a passphrase or PIN"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrSyncBullet3": "Tap Beam via AirQR, and receive it on the new phone with the AirQR receiver.",
  "@helpGuideAirQrSyncBullet3": {
    "description": "AirQR guide: sending the sync package"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrSyncBullet4": "On the new phone, type the same passphrase or PIN and tap Decrypt & Sync.",
  "@helpGuideAirQrSyncBullet4": {
    "description": "AirQR guide: opening the sync package on the new phone"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrSecurityTitle": "Why it is private",
  "@helpGuideAirQrSecurityTitle": {
    "description": "AirQR guide section heading: why AirQR is private"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrSecurityBullet1": "No radio signals are used: no Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, mobile data or internet.",
  "@helpGuideAirQrSecurityBullet1": {
    "description": "AirQR guide: no radio signals are used"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrSecurityBullet2": "Nobody can catch the data over a network. Only a camera that can see the screen can read it.",
  "@helpGuideAirQrSecurityBullet2": {
    "description": "AirQR guide: only a camera that sees the screen can read it"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrSecurityBullet3": "Useful for passwords, keys and other private data you do not want to send online.",
  "@helpGuideAirQrSecurityBullet3": {
    "description": "AirQR guide: good for private data"
  },
  "helpGuideAirQrTip": "Tip: Turn the sending phone's brightness up and hold the receiving phone steady. If parts keep going missing, lower the speed.",
  "@helpGuideAirQrTip": {
    "description": "Tip at the end of the AirQR guide"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyName": "Link safety checks",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyName": {
    "description": "Help hub card title for the link safety guide"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetySummary": "How the app checks every link before you open it, and what the result means.",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetySummary": {
    "description": "Help hub card summary for the link safety guide"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyIntro": "Scam QR codes often lead to fake websites. So before you open any link, the app checks it in up to six ways. The first four checks always run on your phone, with no internet.",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyIntro": {
    "description": "Opening paragraph of the link safety guide"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyLayersTitle": "The six checks",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyLayersTitle": {
    "description": "Link safety guide section heading: the six checks"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyLayersBullet1": "1. Safe connection: is the link using secure HTTPS? Does it hide strange or invisible characters?",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyLayersBullet1": {
    "description": "Link safety check 1: secure connection and hidden characters"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyLayersBullet2": "2. Lookalike letters: some fake sites use letters from other alphabets that look the same, for example a Cyrillic \"а\" in place of a normal \"a\".",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyLayersBullet2": {
    "description": "Link safety check 2: lookalike letters from other alphabets"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyLayersBullet3": "3. Odd web addresses: risky endings (such as .xyz or .top), too many parts in the name, or names made of random letters.",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyLayersBullet3": {
    "description": "Link safety check 3: odd web addresses"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyLayersBullet4": "4. Number addresses and odd ports: links that use a raw number (an IP address) or an unusual port, which normal shops and banks do not use.",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyLayersBullet4": {
    "description": "Link safety check 4: number addresses and odd ports"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyLayersBullet5": "5. Online check of the site (optional): follows short links (like bit.ly) to see where they really go, and checks the site's security certificate. Runs only if you turn on Active online checks.",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyLayersBullet5": {
    "description": "Link safety check 5: optional online check of the site"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyLayersBullet6": "6. Known-bad lists (optional): asks services such as Google Safe Browsing whether the link is a known scam or virus site. Runs only if you set it up.",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyLayersBullet6": {
    "description": "Link safety check 6: optional lists of known bad sites"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyVerdictsTitle": "Reading the result",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyVerdictsTitle": {
    "description": "Link safety guide section heading: reading the result"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyVerdictsBullet1": "No issues found: the link passed every check that ran. Still, trust only sources you know.",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyVerdictsBullet1": {
    "description": "Link safety guide: what No issues found means"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyVerdictsBullet2": "Issues found: the app shows which checks failed. Tap See details to read why.",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyVerdictsBullet2": {
    "description": "Link safety guide: what issues found means and See details"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyVerdictsBullet3": "If you still open a risky link, the app asks you first. Tap Open Anyway only if you trust the source.",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyVerdictsBullet3": {
    "description": "Link safety guide: opening a risky link asks first"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyVerdictsBullet4": "Tap Re-check to run the checks again, for example after you go online.",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyVerdictsBullet4": {
    "description": "Link safety guide: the Re-check button"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyPrivacyTitle": "Private mode and online checks",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyPrivacyTitle": {
    "description": "Link safety guide section heading: private mode and active online checks"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyPrivacyBullet1": "By default, the app never contacts the website itself. The site cannot see your phone or your IP address (your internet address).",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyPrivacyBullet1": {
    "description": "Link safety guide: by default the site itself is never contacted"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyPrivacyBullet2": "If you turn on Active online checks in Settings > Privacy & probing, the app visits the site to follow short links and check its certificate. This finds more, but the site can see your IP address.",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyPrivacyBullet2": {
    "description": "Link safety guide: what turning on active online checks does"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyPrivacyBullet3": "With Active online checks on, the result can also show a safe preview of the page. Scripts and trackers are removed first, so nothing on the page can run. Tap Show preview or Inspect page.",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyPrivacyBullet3": {
    "description": "Link safety guide: the safe page preview"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyProvidersTitle": "Extra online checkers",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyProvidersTitle": {
    "description": "Link safety guide section heading: extra online checkers"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyProvidersBullet1": "In Settings > URL Safety Providers you can turn on more checkers. PhishTank and OpenPhish need no account.",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyProvidersBullet1": {
    "description": "Link safety guide: checkers that need no account"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyProvidersBullet2": "Google Safe Browsing, VirusTotal and URLhaus need your own free key. See the guide \"Online checker setup\".",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyProvidersBullet2": {
    "description": "Link safety guide: checkers that need your own key"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyProvidersBullet3": "These checkers get only the link you scanned. OpenPhish works differently: the app downloads its list and checks on your phone. All of them are off until you turn them on.",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyProvidersBullet3": {
    "description": "Link safety guide: what the online checkers receive"
  },
  "helpGuideUrlSafetyTip": "Tip: A good result is not a promise. Scammers make new sites every day. If a payment or login page looks odd, close it.",
  "@helpGuideUrlSafetyTip": {
    "description": "Tip at the end of the link safety guide"
  },
  "helpGuideQuishingName": "QuishingGuard: fake sticker codes",
  "@helpGuideQuishingName": {
    "description": "Help hub card title for the QuishingGuard guide"
  },
  "helpGuideQuishingSummary": "Spot QR codes that may be fake stickers placed over real ones.",
  "@helpGuideQuishingSummary": {
    "description": "Help hub card summary for the QuishingGuard guide"
  },
  "helpGuideQuishingIntro": "\"Quishing\" means QR phishing. Scammers stick their own QR code over the real one, on parking meters, menus, shop counters and posters, so that your payment or login goes to them.",
  "@helpGuideQuishingIntro": {
    "description": "Opening paragraph of the QuishingGuard guide"
  },
  "helpGuideQuishingCvTitle": "What QuishingGuard shows",
  "@helpGuideQuishingCvTitle": {
    "description": "QuishingGuard guide section heading: what QuishingGuard shows"
  },
  "helpGuideQuishingCvBullet1": "When you scan a link or a payment code with the camera, the result screen shows a small QuishingGuard card: Fake sticker check.",
  "@helpGuideQuishingCvBullet1": {
    "description": "QuishingGuard guide: when and where the fake-sticker check card appears"
  },
  "helpGuideQuishingCvBullet2": "Tap it to open a short list of checks. The app does not look for stickers in the picture and gives no score, so it cannot tell you that a code is safe.",
  "@helpGuideQuishingCvBullet2": {
    "description": "QuishingGuard guide: the card lists hand checks; no image check and no score"
  },
  "helpGuideQuishingCvBullet3": "The card does not appear for photos, the clipboard, screen scans or plain text, because those codes are not stuck on a wall.",
  "@helpGuideQuishingCvBullet3": {
    "description": "QuishingGuard guide: the card is not shown for photos, clipboard, screen scans or plain text"
  },
  "helpGuideQuishingForensicTitle": "What you should do",
  "@helpGuideQuishingForensicTitle": {
    "description": "QuishingGuard guide section heading: what you should do"
  },
  "helpGuideQuishingForensicBullet1": "Look at the code and feel it with your finger. A sticker on top often has raised edges or sits crooked.",
  "@helpGuideQuishingForensicBullet1": {
    "description": "QuishingGuard guide: look at and feel the code"
  },
  "helpGuideQuishingForensicBullet2": "Before you pay, check that the name on the payment screen matches the shop.",
  "@helpGuideQuishingForensicBullet2": {
    "description": "QuishingGuard guide: check the payee name before paying"
  },
  "helpGuideQuishingForensicBullet3": "If in doubt, ask the staff, or type the website address yourself instead.",
  "@helpGuideQuishingForensicBullet3": {
    "description": "QuishingGuard guide: ask the staff or type the address yourself"
  },
  "helpGuideQuishingTip": "Tip: QuishingGuard is a helper, not a promise. Your own eyes and fingers are the best check.",
  "@helpGuideQuishingTip": {
    "description": "Tip at the end of the QuishingGuard guide"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingName": "Online checker setup",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingName": {
    "description": "Help hub card title for the online checker setup guide"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingSummary": "Turn on extra link checks, and get a free key for Google Safe Browsing.",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingSummary": {
    "description": "Help hub card summary for the online checker setup guide"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingIntro": "Online checkers compare a scanned link with lists of known scam and virus sites. They are optional. The app's own checks work without them.",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingIntro": {
    "description": "Opening paragraph of the online checker setup guide"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingBuiltInTitle": "No account needed",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingBuiltInTitle": {
    "description": "Online checker guide section heading: checkers with no account"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingBuiltInBullet1": "Open Settings > URL Safety Providers.",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingBuiltInBullet1": {
    "description": "Online checker guide: where the checkers are"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingBuiltInBullet2": "Turn on Enable PhishTank to check links against PhishTank's list of scam sites.",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingBuiltInBullet2": {
    "description": "Online checker guide: turning on PhishTank"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingBuiltInBullet3": "Turn on Use OpenPhish feed. The app downloads OpenPhish's list and checks links on your phone. Tap Refresh feed now to get the latest list.",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingBuiltInBullet3": {
    "description": "Online checker guide: turning on and refreshing OpenPhish"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingKeyTitle": "Get a free Google Safe Browsing key",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingKeyTitle": {
    "description": "Online checker guide section heading: getting a Google Safe Browsing key"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingKeyStep1": "1. In a browser, open console.cloud.google.com and sign in with a Google account.",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingKeyStep1": {
    "description": "Safe Browsing key step 1: open the Google Cloud console"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingKeyStep2": "2. Create a new project. Any name is fine, for example \"QR safety\".",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingKeyStep2": {
    "description": "Safe Browsing key step 2: create a project"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingKeyStep3": "3. Go to APIs & Services > Library, search for \"Safe Browsing API\" and tap Enable.",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingKeyStep3": {
    "description": "Safe Browsing key step 3: turn on the Safe Browsing API"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingKeyStep4": "4. Go to APIs & Services > Credentials, tap Create credentials and choose API key.",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingKeyStep4": {
    "description": "Safe Browsing key step 4: create an API key"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingKeyStep5": "5. Copy the key. In the app, open Settings > URL Safety Providers, paste it into the Google Safe Browsing box and tap Save API Key.",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingKeyStep5": {
    "description": "Safe Browsing key step 5: paste the key into the app"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingOtherTitle": "Other services with a key",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingOtherTitle": {
    "description": "Online checker guide section heading: other services that need a key"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingOtherBullet1": "VirusTotal and URLhaus work the same way. Make a free account on their website, copy your key, and paste it under Your API Keys. The app shows where to get each key.",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingOtherBullet1": {
    "description": "Online checker guide: VirusTotal and URLhaus keys"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingOtherBullet2": "These free keys are for personal, non-commercial use.",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingOtherBullet2": {
    "description": "Online checker guide: free keys are for personal use"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingOtherBullet3": "Each service has a daily limit, and the app shows how many checks you have used today. In this app, Safe Browsing allows up to 10,000 a day and VirusTotal 500 a day.",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingOtherBullet3": {
    "description": "Online checker guide: daily limits and the usage counter"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingPrivacyTitle": "Your keys are safe",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingPrivacyTitle": {
    "description": "Online checker guide section heading: your keys are safe"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingPrivacyBullet1": "Your keys are kept in Android's secure, locked storage on this phone, and are never shared.",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingPrivacyBullet1": {
    "description": "Online checker guide: keys are kept in secure storage"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingPrivacyBullet2": "Only the link you scanned is sent to the service. Nothing else about you is sent.",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingPrivacyBullet2": {
    "description": "Online checker guide: only the scanned link is sent"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingPrivacyBullet3": "You can delete a key at any time. The app then simply skips that check.",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingPrivacyBullet3": {
    "description": "Online checker guide: deleting a key"
  },
  "helpGuideSafeBrowsingTip": "Tip: You do not need any key to stay safe. The app's own checks always run, even with no internet.",
  "@helpGuideSafeBrowsingTip": {
    "description": "Tip at the end of the online checker setup guide"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsName": "Smart actions",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsName": {
    "description": "Help hub card title for the smart actions guide"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsSummary": "One-tap buttons for Wi-Fi, payments, contacts, events, phone numbers, products and more.",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsSummary": {
    "description": "Help hub card summary for the smart actions guide"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsIntro": "The app understands what a code holds and shows a card with the right buttons. For example, a Wi-Fi code gets a Connect button, and a phone number gets a Call button.",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsIntro": {
    "description": "Opening paragraph of the smart actions guide"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsWifiTitle": "Wi-Fi",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsWifiTitle": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide section heading: Wi-Fi codes"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsWifiBullet1": "Shows the network name and its type of security. Tap the eye button to show or hide the password, or copy it.",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsWifiBullet1": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide: what a Wi-Fi card shows"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsWifiBullet2": "Tap Connect to Wi-Fi. Android may ask you to confirm. If your phone does not allow a direct connection, the password is copied so you can paste it in your Wi-Fi settings.",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsWifiBullet2": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide: connecting to a Wi-Fi network"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsPaymentsTitle": "Payments",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsPaymentsTitle": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide section heading: payment codes"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsPaymentsBullet1": "UPI codes show who you are paying and the amount. Tap Pay with UPI app to open your UPI app (such as Google Pay, PhonePe, Paytm or BHIM) with the details filled in.",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsPaymentsBullet1": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide: paying with a UPI code"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsPaymentsBullet2": "If the code has no amount, the app asks you to type it first.",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsPaymentsBullet2": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide: codes with no amount"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsPaymentsBullet3": "This app never takes or sends money by itself. You confirm every payment in your UPI app.",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsPaymentsBullet3": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide: the app never moves money itself"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsPaymentsBullet4": "Crypto wallet codes (Bitcoin, Ethereum, Solana) and SEPA bank transfer codes show the address, which you can copy.",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsPaymentsBullet4": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide: crypto and SEPA payment codes"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsTotpTitle": "Two-step login codes (2FA)",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsTotpTitle": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide section heading: two-step login codes"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsTotpBullet1": "Websites often show a QR code when you turn on two-step login. Scanning it shows a 6-digit code that changes every 30 seconds, with a timer.",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsTotpBullet1": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide: what a 2FA setup code shows"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsTotpBullet2": "Tap Add to authenticator to save it in your authenticator app, such as Google or Microsoft Authenticator.",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsTotpBullet2": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide: adding the code to an authenticator app"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsTotpBullet3": "Keep this kind of code private. Anyone who scans it can make your login codes.",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsTotpBullet3": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide: keep 2FA setup codes private"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsContactsTitle": "Contacts and events",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsContactsTitle": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide section heading: contacts and events"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsContactsBullet1": "Contact codes (vCard or MeCard) show the name, phone, email and company. Tap Save to Contacts, or call or email straight away.",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsContactsBullet1": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide: contact codes"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsContactsBullet2": "Event codes show the title, time and place. Tap Add to calendar.",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsContactsBullet2": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide: event codes"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsOtherTitle": "Phone, messages, maps and more",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsOtherTitle": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide section heading: phone, messages, email, maps, products and books"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsOtherBullet1": "Phone number: tap Call. Text message: tap Send Message, and the message is filled in for you. Email: tap Send Email.",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsOtherBullet1": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide: phone, SMS and email codes"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsOtherBullet2": "Location: tap Open in Maps to see the place or get directions.",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsOtherBullet2": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide: location codes"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsOtherBullet3": "App link: tap Open in App to open the matching app, if it is installed.",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsOtherBullet3": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide: app link codes"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsOtherBullet4": "Product barcode: tap Food Info to look up food details, or Search Web.",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsOtherBullet4": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide: product barcodes"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsOtherBullet5": "Book (ISBN) barcode: look the book up on Google Books or Open Library.",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsOtherBullet5": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide: book (ISBN) barcodes"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsOtherBullet6": "Web links open in your browser only after the safety check has run.",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsOtherBullet6": {
    "description": "Smart actions guide: links open only after the safety check"
  },
  "helpGuideSmartPayloadsTip": "Tip: Before you pay with a UPI code, check that the name on the card matches the shop or person you want to pay.",
  "@helpGuideSmartPayloadsTip": {
    "description": "Tip at the end of the smart actions guide"
  },
  "helpGuideHiddenName": "Hidden and locked codes",
  "@helpGuideHiddenName": {
    "description": "Help hub card title for the guide on hidden and locked codes"
  },
  "helpGuideHiddenSummary": "Open QR codes that carry a secret message or locked data.",
  "@helpGuideHiddenSummary": {
    "description": "Help hub card summary for the guide on hidden and locked codes"
  },
  "helpGuideHiddenIntro": "Some QR codes carry private data that is locked with a passphrase. The app spots these codes and lets you unlock them, right on your phone.",
  "@helpGuideHiddenIntro": {
    "description": "Opening paragraph of the guide on hidden and locked codes"
  },
  "helpGuideHiddenStegoTitle": "StegoQR: a code with a hidden message",
  "@helpGuideHiddenStegoTitle": {
    "description": "Locked codes guide section heading: StegoQR codes"
  },
  "helpGuideHiddenStegoBullet1": "A StegoQR code shows ordinary public text to everyone, and hides a second, secret message inside it.",
  "@helpGuideHiddenStegoBullet1": {
    "description": "Locked codes guide: what a StegoQR code is"
  },
  "helpGuideHiddenStegoBullet2": "When you scan one, the result shows StegoQR found. The public text is shown as usual.",
  "@helpGuideHiddenStegoBullet2": {
    "description": "Locked codes guide: what you see when you scan a StegoQR code"
  },
  "helpGuideHiddenStegoBullet3": "To see the secret, type the passphrase and tap Unlock. The person who made the code must give you the passphrase.",
  "@helpGuideHiddenStegoBullet3": {
    "description": "Locked codes guide: unlocking with the passphrase"
  },
  "helpGuideHiddenStegoBullet4": "Biometric Unlock asks for your fingerprint or face as well as the passphrase.",
  "@helpGuideHiddenStegoBullet4": {
    "description": "Locked codes guide: biometric unlock"
  },
  "helpGuideHiddenStegoBullet5": "After unlocking, you can copy or share the secret.",
  "@helpGuideHiddenStegoBullet5": {
    "description": "Locked codes guide: copying or sharing the secret"
  },
  "helpGuideHiddenOtherTitle": "Other locked codes",
  "@helpGuideHiddenOtherTitle": {
    "description": "Locked codes guide section heading: other locked codes"
  },
  "helpGuideHiddenOtherBullet1": "AirQR transfer codes: type the session code shown on the sending phone.",
  "@helpGuideHiddenOtherBullet1": {
    "description": "Locked codes guide: AirQR transfer codes and the session code"
  },
  "helpGuideHiddenOtherBullet2": "Encrypted JSON codes and other locked text: tap Decrypt Payload and type the passphrase.",
  "@helpGuideHiddenOtherBullet2": {
    "description": "Locked codes guide: encrypted JSON and other locked text"
  },
  "helpGuideHiddenOtherBullet3": "Advanced (Salt / IV) is only for codes made by other tools that need extra settings. Most people never need it.",
  "@helpGuideHiddenOtherBullet3": {
    "description": "Locked codes guide: the advanced salt and IV fields"
  },
  "helpGuideHiddenSafetyTitle": "Good to know",
  "@helpGuideHiddenSafetyTitle": {
    "description": "Locked codes guide section heading: good to know"
  },
  "helpGuideHiddenSafetyBullet1": "Unlocking happens on your phone. The passphrase and the secret are never sent anywhere.",
  "@helpGuideHiddenSafetyBullet1": {
    "description": "Locked codes guide: unlocking happens on the phone"
  },
  "helpGuideHiddenSafetyBullet2": "A wrong passphrase just shows an error. Check the spelling, capital letters and spaces, and try again.",
  "@helpGuideHiddenSafetyBullet2": {
    "description": "Locked codes guide: what to do after a wrong passphrase"
  },
  "helpGuideHiddenSafetyBullet3": "This app can open these codes, but it does not make them.",
  "@helpGuideHiddenSafetyBullet3": {
    "description": "Locked codes guide: the app reads these codes but cannot make them"
  },
  "helpGuideHiddenTip": "Tip: Share the passphrase in a different way from the code, for example by phone call. Never write it next to the code.",
  "@helpGuideHiddenTip": {
    "description": "Tip at the end of the guide on hidden and locked codes"
  },
  "helpGuideHistoryName": "History, backups and privacy",
  "@helpGuideHistoryName": {
    "description": "Help hub card title for the history guide"
  },
  "helpGuideHistorySummary": "Find old scans, add notes, export or back up your history, and lock the app.",
  "@helpGuideHistorySummary": {
    "description": "Help hub card summary for the history guide"
  },
  "helpGuideHistoryIntro": "Every scan is saved in the History tab on your phone, in a locked (encrypted) store. Nothing is uploaded.",
  "@helpGuideHistoryIntro": {
    "description": "Opening paragraph of the history guide"
  },
  "helpGuideHistoryManageTitle": "Find and manage scans",
  "@helpGuideHistoryManageTitle": {
    "description": "History guide section heading: finding and managing scans"
  },
  "helpGuideHistoryManageBullet1": "Type in the search box to find scans by their content, type or notes.",
  "@helpGuideHistoryManageBullet1": {
    "description": "History guide: the search box"
  },
  "helpGuideHistoryManageBullet2": "Use the filter chips to show only links, Wi-Fi, contacts, products and so on. Tap the star on a scan to add it to Starred.",
  "@helpGuideHistoryManageBullet2": {
    "description": "History guide: filter chips and starring a scan"
  },
  "helpGuideHistoryManageBullet3": "Tap a scan to see all its details: full content, safety score and time. You can add notes and a place, or copy, share or delete it.",
  "@helpGuideHistoryManageBullet3": {
    "description": "History guide: the details sheet of a scan"
  },
  "helpGuideHistoryManageBullet4": "Clear All deletes your whole history. This cannot be undone, so make a backup first.",
  "@helpGuideHistoryManageBullet4": {
    "description": "History guide: clearing all history"
  },
  "helpGuideHistoryBackupTitle": "Export and backup",
  "@helpGuideHistoryBackupTitle": {
    "description": "History guide section heading: export and backup"
  },
  "helpGuideHistoryBackupBullet1": "Tap the Export / Backup button at the top of the History tab.",
  "@helpGuideHistoryBackupBullet1": {
    "description": "History guide: opening export and backup"
  },
  "helpGuideHistoryBackupBullet2": "Export Records saves a copy as CSV (for Excel or Sheets), JSON, text or PDF. These files are not locked: anyone with the file can read your scans, so the app asks you first.",
  "@helpGuideHistoryBackupBullet2": {
    "description": "History guide: plain exports are not locked"
  },
  "helpGuideHistoryBackupBullet3": "Encrypted backup is the safe way to keep a copy. Type a passphrase and tap Create backup, then save or share the file.",
  "@helpGuideHistoryBackupBullet3": {
    "description": "History guide: making an encrypted backup"
  },
  "helpGuideHistoryBackupBullet4": "To restore, open Restore Backup, paste the text from your backup file, type the same passphrase and tap Restore history.",
  "@helpGuideHistoryBackupBullet4": {
    "description": "History guide: restoring an encrypted backup"
  },
  "helpGuideHistoryBiometricsTitle": "App lock and screenshot guard",
  "@helpGuideHistoryBiometricsTitle": {
    "description": "History guide section heading: app lock and screenshot guard"
  },
  "helpGuideHistoryBiometricsBullet1": "App lock: turn it on in Settings > Privacy & probing. The app then asks for your fingerprint, face or screen lock when it opens, and after you have been away for 30 seconds.",
  "@helpGuideHistoryBiometricsBullet1": {
    "description": "History guide: the app lock"
  },
  "helpGuideHistoryBiometricsBullet2": "Screenshot guard: stops screenshots and screen recording on screens with scans, history, secrets or keys. These screens also look blank in the recent apps list. Turn it on or off in Settings > Privacy & probing.",
  "@helpGuideHistoryBiometricsBullet2": {
    "description": "History guide: the screenshot guard"
  },
  "helpGuideHistoryBiometricsBullet3": "To move your history to a new phone, use AirQR Optical Sync. See the AirQR guide.",
  "@helpGuideHistoryBiometricsBullet3": {
    "description": "History guide: moving history to a new phone"
  },
  "helpGuideHistoryTip": "Tip: Make an encrypted backup before you reset or change your phone. Keep the passphrase somewhere safe. Without it, the backup cannot be opened.",
  "@helpGuideHistoryTip": {
    "description": "Tip at the end of the history guide"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsName": "Settings and personal touch",
  "@helpGuideSettingsName": {
    "description": "Help hub card title for the settings guide"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsSummary": "Change the look, language and sounds, see permissions, save battery, and delete your data.",
  "@helpGuideSettingsSummary": {
    "description": "Help hub card summary for the settings guide"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsIntro": "To open Settings, go to the Scan screen, tap More options and choose Settings. Here is what each part does.",
  "@helpGuideSettingsIntro": {
    "description": "Opening paragraph of the settings guide"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsLookTitle": "Look and language",
  "@helpGuideSettingsLookTitle": {
    "description": "Settings guide section heading: look and language"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsLookBullet1": "Appearance > Theme Mode: System, Light, Dark or OLED. OLED is pure black and saves battery on OLED screens.",
  "@helpGuideSettingsLookBullet1": {
    "description": "Settings guide: theme mode choices"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsLookBullet2": "Accent & colors: pick a main colour, or turn on Dynamic colors to match your wallpaper (Android 12 and newer).",
  "@helpGuideSettingsLookBullet2": {
    "description": "Settings guide: accent colour and dynamic colours"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsLookBullet3": "Text size & font: choose the font. The text size follows the text size you set for your phone.",
  "@helpGuideSettingsLookBullet3": {
    "description": "Settings guide: font and text size"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsLookBullet4": "Scan Overlay Style: choose how the scan frame looks.",
  "@helpGuideSettingsLookBullet4": {
    "description": "Settings guide: scan frame style"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsLookBullet5": "Language: choose System default, English, Malayalam (മലയാളം) or Sanskrit (संस्कृतम्). The app changes at once, with no restart.",
  "@helpGuideSettingsLookBullet5": {
    "description": "Settings guide: the language picker"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsFeedbackTitle": "Scan feedback",
  "@helpGuideSettingsFeedbackTitle": {
    "description": "Settings guide section heading: scan feedback"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsFeedbackBullet1": "Choose whether the phone vibrates, beeps, or plays a short animation when a code is read.",
  "@helpGuideSettingsFeedbackBullet1": {
    "description": "Settings guide: vibration, beep and animation after a scan"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsPrivacyTitle": "Privacy & probing",
  "@helpGuideSettingsPrivacyTitle": {
    "description": "Settings guide section heading: privacy and probing"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsPrivacyBullet1": "Active online checks: off unless you turn it on. See the Link safety guide.",
  "@helpGuideSettingsPrivacyBullet1": {
    "description": "Settings guide: the active online checks switch"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsPrivacyBullet2": "App lock and Screenshot guard: see the History, backups and privacy guide.",
  "@helpGuideSettingsPrivacyBullet2": {
    "description": "Settings guide: app lock and screenshot guard"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsPrivacyBullet3": "Delete all data: removes your scan history, saved keys and all settings from this phone. This cannot be undone.",
  "@helpGuideSettingsPrivacyBullet3": {
    "description": "Settings guide: delete all data"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsOtherTitle": "Other settings",
  "@helpGuideSettingsOtherTitle": {
    "description": "Settings guide section heading: other settings"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsOtherBullet1": "URL Safety Providers: turn on extra online link checkers.",
  "@helpGuideSettingsOtherBullet1": {
    "description": "Settings guide: URL safety providers"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsOtherBullet2": "AirQR Optical Sync: move your history and settings to another phone.",
  "@helpGuideSettingsOtherBullet2": {
    "description": "Settings guide: AirQR optical sync"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsOtherBullet3": "Scan bubble: a floating button to scan codes in other apps.",
  "@helpGuideSettingsOtherBullet3": {
    "description": "Settings guide: the scan bubble"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsOtherBullet4": "Permissions: a plain list of what the app may use, and why. The app asks for each one only when a feature needs it.",
  "@helpGuideSettingsOtherBullet4": {
    "description": "Settings guide: the permissions screen"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsOtherBullet5": "Features lists everything the app can do. Welcome Tour shows the first-start introduction again. About shows the app version and licences.",
  "@helpGuideSettingsOtherBullet5": {
    "description": "Settings guide: features, welcome tour and about"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsBatteryTitle": "Saving battery",
  "@helpGuideSettingsBatteryTitle": {
    "description": "Settings guide section heading: saving battery"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsBatteryBullet1": "The camera turns off as soon as you leave the Scan screen or the app.",
  "@helpGuideSettingsBatteryBullet1": {
    "description": "Settings guide: the camera turns off on its own"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsBatteryBullet2": "Choose 720p in Camera adjustments to use less power.",
  "@helpGuideSettingsBatteryBullet2": {
    "description": "Settings guide: choose 720p to use less power"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsBatteryBullet3": "Turn off the Scan bubble when you do not need it.",
  "@helpGuideSettingsBatteryBullet3": {
    "description": "Settings guide: turn off the scan bubble when not needed"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsBatteryBullet4": "Use the OLED theme on phones with an OLED screen.",
  "@helpGuideSettingsBatteryBullet4": {
    "description": "Settings guide: the OLED theme saves battery"
  },
  "helpGuideSettingsTip": "Tip: Not sure where something is? Every guide here names the button to tap.",
  "@helpGuideSettingsTip": {
    "description": "Tip at the end of the settings guide"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqName": "FAQ and problems",
  "@helpGuideFaqName": {
    "description": "Help hub card title for the FAQ"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqSummary": "Answers to common questions, and fixes when something does not work.",
  "@helpGuideFaqSummary": {
    "description": "Help hub card summary for the FAQ"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqIntro": "Quick answers to common questions, and what to do when something does not work.",
  "@helpGuideFaqIntro": {
    "description": "Opening paragraph of the FAQ"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqQuestionsTitle": "Common questions",
  "@helpGuideFaqQuestionsTitle": {
    "description": "FAQ section heading: common questions"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqQuestion1": "Does the app work without internet?\nYes. Reading codes, the first four link checks and QuishingGuard all work offline. Only the optional online checks need the internet.",
  "@helpGuideFaqQuestion1": {
    "description": "FAQ question and answer: does the app work offline (question, newline, answer)"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqQuestion2": "Are my camera pictures sent anywhere?\nNo. Pictures are read on your phone and are never saved or uploaded.",
  "@helpGuideFaqQuestion2": {
    "description": "FAQ question and answer: are camera pictures sent anywhere"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqQuestion3": "Does the app collect data about me?\nNo. There are no ads, no tracking and no analytics. Your history stays on your phone.",
  "@helpGuideFaqQuestion3": {
    "description": "FAQ question and answer: does the app collect data about the user"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqQuestion4": "Why does the app ask for a permission?\nOnly when you use a feature that needs it, such as the camera for scanning. See Settings > Permissions for the full list.",
  "@helpGuideFaqQuestion4": {
    "description": "FAQ question and answer: why the app asks for a permission"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqQuestion5": "How do I change the language?\nGo to Settings > Language. The app changes at once.",
  "@helpGuideFaqQuestion5": {
    "description": "FAQ question and answer: how to change the language"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqQuestion6": "How do I delete everything?\nGo to Settings > Privacy & probing > Delete all data. You can also delete single scans in History.",
  "@helpGuideFaqQuestion6": {
    "description": "FAQ question and answer: how to delete everything"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqQuestion7": "A link I trust is marked unsafe. Why?\nThe checks look for warning signs, and some real sites have them too. If you are sure about the source, you can still open it.",
  "@helpGuideFaqQuestion7": {
    "description": "FAQ question and answer: why a trusted link is marked unsafe"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqQuestion8": "Does the app use a lot of battery?\nNo. The camera stops as soon as you leave the Scan screen. See the Settings guide for more battery tips.",
  "@helpGuideFaqQuestion8": {
    "description": "FAQ question and answer: battery use"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqCameraTitle": "When a code will not scan",
  "@helpGuideFaqCameraTitle": {
    "description": "FAQ section heading: when a code will not scan"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqCameraBullet1": "Clean the camera lens and hold the phone about 15 to 20 cm (6 to 8 inches) from the code.",
  "@helpGuideFaqCameraBullet1": {
    "description": "FAQ: clean the lens and hold the phone at the right distance"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqCameraBullet2": "In a dark place, turn on the flash. For a shiny code, tilt the phone a little to remove the glare.",
  "@helpGuideFaqCameraBullet2": {
    "description": "FAQ: dark places and shiny codes"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqCameraBullet3": "For a small or far-away code, use the zoom slider or Distance Scan Assist, instead of moving very close.",
  "@helpGuideFaqCameraBullet3": {
    "description": "FAQ: small or far-away codes"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqCameraBullet4": "For a light code on a dark background, turn on Invert colors in Camera adjustments.",
  "@helpGuideFaqCameraBullet4": {
    "description": "FAQ: light codes on a dark background"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqCameraBullet5": "For a damaged or faded code, try Brightness and Contrast in Camera adjustments, or take a photo and scan it from the gallery.",
  "@helpGuideFaqCameraBullet5": {
    "description": "FAQ: damaged or faded codes"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqFixTitle": "Other problems",
  "@helpGuideFaqFixTitle": {
    "description": "FAQ section heading: other problems"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqFixBullet1": "Camera does not open: if you said no to the camera, go to Android Settings > Apps > SreerajP QR Studio > Permissions > Camera and choose Allow.",
  "@helpGuideFaqFixBullet1": {
    "description": "FAQ: the camera does not open because permission was refused"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqFixBullet2": "Wi-Fi will not connect: copy the password and join the network in your phone's Wi-Fi settings.",
  "@helpGuideFaqFixBullet2": {
    "description": "FAQ: Wi-Fi will not connect"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqFixBullet3": "Payment app does not open: make sure a UPI app is installed. You can also copy the UPI ID.",
  "@helpGuideFaqFixBullet3": {
    "description": "FAQ: the payment app does not open"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqFixBullet4": "Scan bubble keeps disappearing: some phones stop apps in the background. Allow this app in your phone's battery settings.",
  "@helpGuideFaqFixBullet4": {
    "description": "FAQ: the scan bubble keeps disappearing"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqFixBullet5": "An online check says Skipped: that checker is turned off, or has no key. Tap Set up in Settings on the result to fix it.",
  "@helpGuideFaqFixBullet5": {
    "description": "FAQ: an online check shows as skipped"
  },
  "helpGuideFaqTip": "Tip: Still stuck? Take a clear photo of the code and scan it from the gallery.",
  "@helpGuideFaqTip": {
    "description": "Tip at the end of the FAQ"
  },
